"pa_1":{"d":7.22,"w":"prof","t":"Hello, Sweeper. Professor Lindqvist, Station Nord-7. I study ice. I did not ask for mines. Nobody asks for mines."},
"pa_10":{"d":7.33,"w":"prof","t":"Your friend from the club called the station. He asked if we have a VIP section. We do. It is the only room with heating."},
"pa_11":{"d":7.95,"w":"prof","t":"In my field, we measure progress in millimetres per century. You are moving much faster than that. Honestly, it is a little upsetting."},
"pa_12":{"d":6.88,"w":"prof","t":"People say the Arctic is empty. It is not empty, Sweeper. It is full of silence. And, as of this week, mines."},
"pa_13":{"d":5.84,"w":"prof","t":"Your health is regenerating. Interesting. Up here, nothing regenerates. Except the paperwork."},
"pa_14":{"d":6.56,"w":"prof","t":"I applied for a grant to study the mines. It was rejected. The committee said the mines were not peer reviewed."},
"pa_15":{"d":7.39,"w":"prof","t":"I am told you have a skill tree. We have no trees up here. We have a skill lichen. It grows one point every forty years."},
"pa_16":{"d":6.24,"w":"prof","t":"Please be careful near the freezer behind you. My entire career is in that freezer. Also my lunch."},
"pa_17":{"d":8.87,"w":"prof","t":"It is now −40° outside. That is the only temperature where Celsius and Fahrenheit agree. It is also where I stop agreeing with anyone."},
"pa_18":{"d":7.1,"w":"prof","t":"Every ice crystal is unique. Every mine is identical. Scientifically, I find that deeply disappointing."},
"pa_19":{"d":8.29,"w":"prof","t":"Command says this is a stealth section. Sweeper, you are following a glowing orange quest marker. In the polar night. They can see you from orbit."},
"pa_2":{"d":5.26,"w":"prof","t":"Fascinating. The mines appear to be hibernating. Please do not wake them. They are grumpy."},
"pa_20":{"d":6.18,"w":"prof","t":"The night here lasts four months. Please try to finish before sunrise. I have already scheduled the press release."},
"pa_21":{"d":7.99,"w":"prof","t":"I used to talk to the penguins out there. Then I remembered that penguins live at the other pole. I still do not know who I was talking to."},
"pa_22":{"d":8.31,"w":"prof","t":"The mines are rising through the permafrost as it thaws. So, in a way, this is a climate story. Please make a note of that in your quest log."},
"pa_23":{"d":7.84,"w":"prof","t":"If you find an ice core with a mine frozen inside it, do not sweep it. Bring it to me. That is not a hazard. That is a publication."},
"pa_24":{"d":8.1,"w":"prof","t":"Field notes, day 4,012. The Sweeper is still here. The mines are fewer. The coffee is frozen solid. Morale is excellent."},
"pa_3":{"d":6.8,"w":"prof","t":"The aurora tonight is spectacular. That green light is the solar wind. That orange light is the quest marker."},
"pa_4":{"d":8.5,"w":"prof","t":"My research shows that 90% of each mine is below the surface, like an iceberg. The other 10% is also below the surface."},
"pa_5":{"d":7.54,"w":"prof","t":"I have been at this station for eleven winters. You are the first visitor who did not ask me if it is cold. Thank you. It is cold."},
"pa_6":{"d":7.14,"w":"prof","t":"Please do not lick the tiles. I know it is tempting. Private Jenkins tried. Private Jenkins is still attached to one."},
"pa_7":{"d":9.63,"w":"prof","t":"These ice cores are 40,000 years old. Every layer is one year. This layer here is the year someone buried mines in my glacier. A very bad year."},
"pa_8":{"d":7.99,"w":"prof","t":"Sweeper, a polar bear has been watching your progress on the station monitors. He seems very invested. Please do not disappoint him."},
"pa_9":{"d":6.35,"w":"prof","t":"I have named all the mines. That one is Ingrid. That one is also Ingrid. I ran out of names quite early."},
